{
  "_comment": [
    "DRAFT bench spec: the handshake rungs ASIC/gls-netlist/bench/",
    "eth_chiplet_fp1505_cc.json still lacks, added to the spec as it stands on",
    "2026-08-19 12:25. NOT APPLIED -- bench/ is owned elsewhere. The design note",
    "is docs/tapeout/57-cpu0-boot-on-the-routed-netlist.md and the signoff stage",
    "that grades these key names is docs/proposed/signoff-gls-netlist.yaml.",
    "",
    "EVERY PROBE BELOW HAS BEEN SIMULATED. They are not proposed from the netlist",
    "text: they were run on this netlist with this flash model on 2026-08-19 and",
    "every one of them fired. The verdict and transcript are captured verbatim in",
    "docs/tapeout/evidence/57-cpu0-boot-verdicts.md section A. What is NOT",
    "verified is this FILE as a whole: the probes were measured in a spec built on",
    "flash/bench/eth_chiplet_fp1505_flashboot.json, and are transplanted here onto",
    "the shipped spec, which had not yet landed when they were measured.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, AND WHY.",
    "",
    "1. NO PROBE ON THE 4-BIT BUS chip_core_remap_ctrl_w. It is declared",
    "   `wire [3:0]` in the routed netlist and bits 0, 1 and 3 appear NOWHERE",
    "   ELSE in the file -- not as a driver, not as a load. cpu1_bootgate is tied",
    "   1'b1 in nanosoc_multicore_soc.sv so bit 1's control fan-out is dead, and",
    "   P&R gave the other three flops' outputs the readback net name",
    "   (chip_core_remap_0_hrdata[n]). So the bus traces as 0xZ -- the UPPER-CASE",
    "   Z of a PARTLY unknown nibble -- even at the instant the bootgate rises,",
    "   and an === against a fully-defined 4-bit literal can never match. Two",
    "   expects written that way shipped for a day as FAIL never and were read as",
    "   a failed handshake. Probe the BIT, and the flop pin.",
    "",
    "2. NO eth_imem_prestaged. The first draft required it, from the firmware's",
    "   description of the sequence. MEASURED: ZERO writes to the eth IMEM macro",
    "   while the bootgate was low, and 220 after it. CPU1 does not pre-stage",
    "   eth's image in this build; CPU0 copies its own. Dropped, not waived.",
    "",
    "3. NO memcheck on the eth IMEM. rf_32k's array is `reg [511:0] mem [0:511]`",
    "   -- 512 rows of 512 bits, column-muxed -- so a word-oriented golden would",
    "   mismatch every row of a PERFECTLY COPIED image.",
    "",
    "4. NO UART BYTE DECODE. There is no UART pad on nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads, and",
    "   trace/expect cannot decode a serial byte. eth_sysctrl_remap_set answers",
    "   the same question structurally; the uart trace below is diagnostic only.",
    "",
    "RUN LENGTH IS LOAD-BEARING. run_cycles here is 440000 = 8.8 ms. The shipped",
    "spec's 250000 ends the simulation at 5.000 ms, and CPU0's post-CRC sysctrl",
    "REMAP store was MEASURED at 5.484510 ms on the probe image (the shipped",
    "image's chain runs ~0.28 ms later throughout). Declaring",
    "eth_sysctrl_remap_set without raising run_cycles produces a red that means",
    "'the clock ran out' and reads as 'the CRC failed'.",
    "",
    "A joint work commissioned on behalf of SoC Labs, under Arm Academic Access",
    "license. Copyright (C) 2026, SoC Labs (www.soclabs.org)"
  ],
